From: MeowArchMobile adbd standalone build
Subject: [PATCH] main.cpp: honor ADBD_NO_AUTH on non-Android hosts

auth_required defaults to true and only Android's ro.adb.secure / userdebug
logic ever clears it. A glibc host has no framework to approve keys, so give
it an escape hatch: ADBD_NO_AUTH=1 disables adbd-side authentication
entirely (the test harness and the USB-FFS bring-up both need it).

Context is exact on purpose. The previous version declared two '#endif'
lines where the file has one '}' plus one '#endif', so patch only matched
with fuzz — and fuzz lets a hunk match at a shifted offset, so every build
re-applied it as a new copy instead of seeing it as already present. That
is how daemon/main.cpp had accumulated 22 identical blocks.

diff --git a/daemon/main.cpp b/daemon/main.cpp
index 931b170..43f2058 100644
--- a/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -233,6 +233,13 @@ int adbd_main() {
     }
 #endif
 
+#if !defined(__ANDROID__)
+    // MeowArchMobile: no framework to approve keys on a glibc host, so give it
+    // an escape hatch — ADBD_NO_AUTH=1 disables adbd-side authentication
+    // entirely (the test harness and the USB-FFS bring-up both need it).
+    if (getenv("ADBD_NO_AUTH")) auth_required = false;
+#endif
+
     // Our external storage path may be different than apps, since
     // we aren't able to bind mount after dropping root.
     const char* adb_external_storage = getenv("ADB_EXTERNAL_STORAGE");
